WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:05.110
Imagine if the internet took hold in China.

00:00:05.121 --> 00:00:07.180
Imagine how freedom would spread

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:10.256
Unrestricted internet access is a source of strength.

00:00:11.346 --> 00:00:14.404
That country has some of the toughest 
internet restrictions in the world.

00:00:14.966 --> 00:00:17.957
The government in China's tightening
up on internet restriction it says

00:00:17.957 --> 00:00:22.450
because of the number of anonymous
postings that poke fun at the government.

00:00:22.954 --> 00:00:27.424
So you think they're ultimately going to be on 
the right side of history the Chinese government?

00:00:27.401 --> 00:00:30.862
I am 100%. For sure because nobody can stop
this technology revolution.

00:00:37.694 --> 00:00:42.233
It's 1987 in West Germany and a
university professor has just got an email.

00:00:42.233 --> 00:00:44.158
It contains one short sentence.

00:00:48.146 --> 00:00:50.895
He's just received the first email from China.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:03.570
But it isn't until 1994 that the internet 
becomes available to the public

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:05.450
under the presidency of Jiang Zemin.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.897
Like many of his compatriots Jiang
is deeply influenced

00:01:08.897 --> 00:01:10.731
by the work of Alvin Toffler 

00:01:10.731 --> 00:01:15.642
an American writer whose book Future Shock
predicts a super-industrial revolution

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:19.103
brought about by the moderation 
and regulation of technology.

00:01:21.177 --> 00:01:23.973
Computers combine facts to make new knowledge

00:01:23.973 --> 00:01:26.710
at such high speed that we cannot absorb it.

00:01:27.713 --> 00:01:30.944
But computers are expensive and 
hardly anyone owns one

00:01:30.944 --> 00:01:33.420
so the internet cafe is born.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.950
It costs around 25 yuan or $3 for an hour.

00:01:54.748 --> 00:02:00.043
In 1995 a former English teacher called Jack Ma 
heads to the U.S. on business.

00:02:00.043 --> 00:02:03.262
While he's there he does a 
web search for the word beer

00:02:03.262 --> 00:02:05.138
are no results about China.

00:02:05.493 --> 00:02:08.553
He returns home and starts 
an online yellow pages.

00:02:09.092 --> 00:02:12.381
You don't make any money,
you've got extraordinary claims

00:02:12.381 --> 00:02:14.117
and yet you make nothing. 

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.180
That's the internet.

00:02:16.547 --> 00:02:23.687
By 1999 the company Tencent releases OICQ
 and Jack Ma creates Alibaba.

00:02:24.374 --> 00:02:28.411
It's the Millennium and the unveiling 
of the Golden Shield project

00:02:28.411 --> 00:02:32.743
which includes a new surveillance system 
made up of content-filtering firewalls.

00:02:32.972 --> 00:02:37.373
The system becomes known around the world 
as the Great Firewall of China.

00:02:54.813 --> 00:02:58.117
It only takes a couple more years 
for China to overtake the U.S.

00:02:58.117 --> 00:03:00.383
and have the world's most Internet users

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.007
Fast forward and it's 2012.

00:03:03.007 --> 00:03:06.483
Xi Jinping is elected general secretary
of the Communist Party

00:03:06.483 --> 00:03:08.833
with a vision of "cyber sovereignty".

00:03:08.833 --> 00:03:12.127
Protecting the country's internet 
from foreign influence.

00:03:19.059 --> 00:03:24.170
Notable restrictions include Winnie the Pooh 
because of comparisons made to Xi Jingping

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.614
and the letter N.

00:03:55.973 --> 00:04:01.754
It doesn't take long for controversial new laws
which "ensure cybersecurity" to appear.

00:04:01.754 --> 00:04:05.421
These grant the government unprecedented
access to foreign companies

00:04:05.421 --> 00:04:08.768
including their hardware and sensitive user data.

00:04:09.914 --> 00:04:15.552
In 2018 Freedom House names China as the
worst country in the world for online freedom.

00:04:15.552 --> 00:04:18.865
But China soon starts exporting
its to take on the Internet

00:04:18.854 --> 00:04:22.498
to countries like Vietnam, Uganda
and Tanzania.

